  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0067155.png\" style=\"width: 143px; height: 135px;\" /></p><p>The effective acceleration due to gravity in the reference frame of the vehicle is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>The angle made by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;with the verticle is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>At the lowest point (shown in the figure), let the speed is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
